/* =====================================================================
   group-photo-core.js — the model for ACTIVITY #131 of the one-by-one
   rebuild: "Ziggy's Odd One Out" → THE GROUP PHOTO (L.1.5.a; all 11
   locales).
   Design: docs/activities-rebuild/designs/131-ziggy-odd-one-out.md
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   A camera that only takes a SHARP group photo when everyone on the bench
   is one kind of thing. The child sends the one that doesn't belong to the
   step and presses the shutter:
   · the right one on the step → the photo is sharp and the group's kind
     word is written under it (or, with "I name it", the child picks the
     name from three tags — never a tag that is true of every member);
   · anyone else → miss 1: a cloudy photo, no name; miss 2: the ones that
     share the kind come out sharp, the kind word is pencilled in, and the
     one that breaks it stays blurred.
   Levels: 1 odd one out (4 seats) · 2 trickier groups (5 seats, a
   look-alike decoy in every round) · 3 what is it made of (4 seats) ·
   4 word groups (5 word cards, rebuilt per locale) · 5 the seat plan:
   three friends × three things, clue cards, X and ✓ stones — a ✓ pushes
   an X into every open cell of its row and column, and lifting it lifts
   only the Xs it pushed; a solved plan is photographed and two true /
   false sentences are read off it.
   DATA is written by a build script. Pure and DOM-free; UMD
   (window.GroupPhotoCore / require()).
   ===================================================================== */
